# What subsub.work publishes: the marketing site and NOTHING ELSE.
#
# wrangler.jsonc serves the repository root ("assets": {"directory": "./"}),
# and with no ignore file that is the whole repository -- the app's source,
# the Worker, the migrations, CLAUDE.md, the business notes. So this is an
# allow-list rather than a deny-list: ignore everything, then name what the
# site is made of. A new file at the root is private until it is added here,
# which is the safe direction to be wrong in.
#
# Read by wrangler with gitignore rules (the `ignore` package), and checked
# by app/scripts/site-assets-test.mjs against the real tree before any deploy.
*
!*/
!/*.html
!/*.png
!/*.webp
!/*.ico
!/*.svg
!/*.webmanifest
!/robots.txt
!/sitemap.xml
!/licensing/**
!/compare/**
!/blog/**
!/check/**
!/handyman-limits/**
